## Getting Started

```powershell
python -m venv .venv
.\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
pip install -e ".[dev]"
pytest
```

## Run Locally

Default data policy:

- Schwab is the preferred market data source when credentials and token are configured.
- yfinance remains the automatic fallback for daily bars and a cached fallback for fundamentals where Schwab does not expose the required field.
- The rectangle scanner rules stay deterministic and provider-agnostic.

CLI:

```powershell
scanner scan-yfinance AAPL MSFT NVDA
```

Classic rectangle profile:

```powershell
scanner scan-yfinance AAPL MSFT NVDA --period 2y --profile "Classic rectangle" --lookback 40 --max-range-pct 0.25
```

S&P 500 universe:

```powershell
scanner scan-universe --universe sp500 --period 2y --profile "Classic rectangle" --lookback 40 --max-range-pct 0.25 --min-score 0.60 --limit 50
```

Overnight cache preload:

```powershell
scanner warm-cache --universe sp500 --period 2y --refresh
```

Preload every supported universe:

```powershell
scanner warm-cache --universe all --period 2y --refresh
```

Check local cache coverage:

```powershell
scanner cache-status --universe sp500 --period 2y
```

CLI with exports:

```powershell
scanner scan-yfinance AAPL MSFT NVDA `
  --output-csv data/exports/latest_scan.csv `
  --output-qx-results data/exports/scanner_results.csv `
  --output-json data/exports/latest_scan.json `
  --chart-dir data/exports/charts `
  --database data/qx.db
```

Backtest:

```powershell
scanner backtest-yfinance AAPL --period 2y --profile "Classic rectangle" --max-range-pct 0.25
scanner backtest-universe --universe sp100 --period 2y --profile "Classic rectangle" --limit 25
```

Optional dashboard:

```powershell
pip install -e ".[app]"
streamlit run src/scanner/ui/streamlit_app.py
```

Schwab setup and token lifecycle notes:

- [Schwab OAuth Token Lifecycle](docs/reference/schwab-oauth-token-lifecycle.md)
